course: dictionary
lesson: 10940
title: Wafer: a biscuit, a bread, or a slice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. «Wafer» can mean a crisp biscuit, a thin piece of bread in church, or a very thin slice. Read the words around it to find the clues.
explain: «Silicon comes from sand made extremely pure; it is melted and a big crystal is slowly pulled out as a cylinder, then sliced into thin shiny discs called wafers.» Words like silicon, crystal and shiny tell you this is about science, not food. So a wafer here is a thin disc.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it talks about ice cream, a wafer is a biscuit. If it talks about church, the wafer is bread. If it talks about thin slices, it means a thin piece. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A wafer is a very thin, light, crisp biscuit, often eaten with ice cream.
fact: «Wafer-thin» means extremely thin.
fact: In many churches, a wafer is a thin, round piece of special bread given at Holy Communion.
fact: In Catholic churches the communion wafer is also called the host.
fact: A wafer can be any very thin slice, like the silicon wafers used to make computer chips.
exercise: Sam eats a wafer with his ice cream. What is a wafer here? | *A very thin, crisp biscuit | A small metal tool | A large, soft loaf of bread | A cold drink
exercise: At the church service, a wafer is given out at Holy Communion. What is the wafer? | *A thin, round piece of special bread | A lit candle | A cup of juice | A piece of wood
exercise: The silicon was sliced into thin shiny discs called wafers. What does wafer mean here? | A tasty cookie | *A very thin slice, like a disc | A loud noise | A sweet drink
test: The sheet of glass was wafer-thin, so it could bend easily. What does wafer-thin mean? | Painted bright red | *Extremely thin | Very heavy | Full of holes
test: Which sentence uses wafer to mean a thin slice? | We ate a wafer with a cup of tea | The priest gave out the wafer at the altar | *The chip is made from a silicon wafer, sliced thin and shiny | The ice cream came with a crisp wafer on the side
exam: Read «The thin wafer on the plate was crisp and light.» What clue tells you wafer means a biscuit here? | *Crisp and light, which describe a biscuit | The word thin, which means dangerous | The word on, which means above | The word plate, because plates only hold cutlery
